  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the strongest configuration so far, while image-only resnet50 (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak in isolation. The central open question for a multimodal profiling study is whether the weak image signal carries complementary morphological information that, when fused with the strong RNA signal, improves over RNA alone. This experiment (config_018: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests that question by taking the best-validated RNA pipeline and adding the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). If it significantly beats 0.591, it confirms multimodal value and justifies further fusion/image-encoder exploration; if it does not, it tells us to focus remaining budget on RNA encoder alternatives (scvi, scgpt) rather than image fusion. This is the highest-information single experiment because its outcome bifurcates the entire remaining search space."
}

